{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For a man I have slain for my wound.</b> Lemech brought the sword and murder into the world, and 'the deeds of the fathers are done by the sons,' for he was the son of Cain, the first murderer. And he begot three sons: the firstborn he taught the craft of herding, according to the natures of animals. The second son he taught the art of music. The third son he taught the instruments of warfare — with swords and spears, and to sharpen bronze. And his wives were afraid of him, that he would die in the punishment of his sin, because he brought murder into the world; therefore he would say to them: כי איש הרגתי לפצעי — 'for a man I have slain for my wound' — or 'a child for my bruise' — that I inflicted upon him, just as Cain did. His intention was to say that a man can kill without a sword, and the sword is not the cause of murder; and even though he introduced its craft into the world, there is no punishment upon him for this, for it is possible to put to death by a death more severe than the sword."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:22.884360849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}